# QuickNote. Both looks.
rec qn-open 1 ipc panels open quickNote TESSERA-TEST
note Material settles in about 0.3 s with at most 1 % overshoot; Glass about 0.4 s with a little more overshoot. Compare QML within 1 frame.
wait 1
shot empty
note Quick note card open with an empty editor; Save button disabled (Material 12 % fill / 38 % text). Same as QML.
rec qn-close 0.4 key -k Escape
note Escape closes in 192 ms, same as QML.
wait 1
ipc panels open quickNote TESSERA-TEST
wait 1
key hello
key -k Escape
wait 1
ipc panels open quickNote TESSERA-TEST
wait 1
shot reopen
note Reopened: "hello" is back in the editor, caret at the end. Save enabled.
# NOTE: Save button at the card's bottom right (position assumed); click on layer surfaces may not register
rec qn-save-press 0.6 ptr move 1180 700 sleep 100 down sleep 400 glide 900 400 100 up
note Material: pressing Save: corners go to 8 and it swells about 6 % in 0.22-0.29 s; Glass: 97 %. Released away so it does not save. Same as QML.
key -M ctrl -k Return -m ctrl
wait 1
shot saved
note Ctrl+Enter saves (a file in the notes folder) and closes the dialog.
ipc panels open quickNote TESSERA-TEST
wait 1
shot empty-again
note After saving, the reopened note is empty.
# FAB at the editor's bottom right (position assumed)
ptr move 1180 620 sleep 200 click
wait 1
rec qn-fab 0.8 ptr move 1180 620 sleep 100 click
note Material FAB: it rounds and the + turns into x with a small overshoot; the items spring out nearest first. Glass has no FAB (nothing happens). Click again: items go back together.
wait 1
shot fab
note FAB state (Material): items visible when open; compare with QML.
ptr move 1180 620 sleep 100 click
ipc panels close
